From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:50:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: turn SQLite encryption on by default, for encriox's
 spike

The launch guard (nsAppRunner.cpp, CheckEncryptionCompatibility) reads
security.storage.encryption.sqlite.enabled in XRE_mainStartup, before
XPCOM and Preferences start, so it sees the YAML's value and no other.
With the switch turned on by a GeckoView embedder's default prefs, the
first start encrypted the profile and wrote its EncryptedDatabases
marker, and the next start was refused, on the S9 (encriox W13).
On by default, the guard and the session agree. An embedder's default
can still turn it off, for a profile of one session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml b/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
index 959aa930ad..af078cfb7e 100644
--- a/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
+++ b/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
@@ -19785,9 +19785,12 @@
 # ciphertext. Read at Connection::initialize, not hot-reloadable.
 # Not locked in encriox's spike (W13), so that the default prefs
 # a GeckoView embedder gives can turn it on, over a fresh profile only.
+# On by default there: the launch guard (nsAppRunner.cpp) reads it before
+# Preferences starts, so it sees this value and nothing else, and refuses a
+# profile that a value from elsewhere encrypted.
 - name: security.storage.encryption.sqlite.enabled
   type: RelaxedAtomicBool
-  value: false
+  value: true
   mirror: always
 
 - name: security.tls13.aes_128_gcm_sha256
